      "id": 1,
      "text": "Manning was founded in 1908 to serve as the seat of Dunn County, itself organized that year.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manning%2C_North_Dakota",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Manning was named after pioneer rancher Dan Manning (1845–1914), who promoted the area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manning%2C_North_Dakota",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Established in 1908 alongside Dunn County, Manning emerged as a planned townsite tied to the anticipated arrival of the Northern Pacific Railroad.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/manning_north_dakota",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The original Dunn County Courthouse, built in 1908, burned in 1914 and was replaced by the current structure, highlighting early growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
